Infinite Gates Privacy Policy

Last updated: October 2, 2026

Infinite Gates ("the App") is developed by twelve52 LLC ("we", "us", or "our"). This Privacy Policy explains how information is collected, used, and disclosed when you use the App on iOS or Android.

Information We Collect
The App itself does not collect, store, or transmit any personal information to our servers. We do not require account creation, and we do not ask for your name, email address, or any other personal details.

Game data such as your heroes, progress, settings, and purchases are stored locally on your device. If you choose to sign in to Apple Game Center or Google Play Games, your progress can also be saved to your own Apple or Google account so you can continue on another device.

Third-Party Services
The App uses the following third-party services that may collect information:

Google AdMob — We display ads through Google AdMob. Google may collect and use data to serve personalized or non-personalized ads, including device identifiers, approximate location derived from your IP address, and usage and diagnostic data. You can review Google's privacy policy at policies.google.com/privacy. On first launch the App asks for your consent where the law requires it, and you can change your choices at any time from Privacy in the App's Settings.

Apple Game Center (iOS) — If you choose to sign in to Game Center, Apple handles your profile, leaderboard, and achievement data according to Apple's privacy policy at apple.com/privacy.

Google Play Games (Android) — If you choose to sign in to Google Play Games, Google handles your profile, leaderboard, achievement, and saved game data according to Google's privacy policy at policies.google.com/privacy.

App Tracking Transparency (iOS) — On iOS 14.5 and later, the App asks your permission before allowing third-party services to track your activity across other apps and websites. You can change this permission at any time in your device's Settings.

In-App Purchases
The App offers optional purchases, including Remove Ads, Crown packs, and the Crown Pass monthly subscription. These transactions are processed entirely by Apple through the App Store or by Google through Google Play. We do not receive or store any payment information.

Children's Privacy
The App is intended for players aged 13 and older. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under the age of 13. The App contains third-party advertising which may collect data as described above.

Data Retention and Deletion
Since we do not collect personal data, there is no personal data on our servers to retain. Local game data remains on your device until you delete the App. Saved games, leaderboard scores, and achievements held in your Apple Game Center or Google Play Games account can be removed through those accounts' settings.

If you would like us to delete any data connected to you, email us at general@twelve52cards.com and we will take care of it.

Your Choices
You can opt out of personalized advertising by adjusting your device settings (iOS: Settings > Privacy > Tracking; Android: Settings > Google > Ads) or from Privacy in the App's Settings. You can also purchase Remove Ads within the App.

Changes to This Policy
We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Any changes will be reflected on this page with an updated revision date.

Contact Us
If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy, please contact us at general@twelve52cards.com
